// EXPECT: PASS
// Precision gain from straight-line strong-overwrite: `fwd` binds the secret param to `r` then
// UNCONDITIONALLY reassigns `r` to a clean constant before returning it — so `fwd` returns nothing
// derived from the secret. A straight-line whole-`Var` reassignment strong-overwrites (the old flow is
// dead), so `fwd` summarizes {} and the send accepts. Weak-union (the former body-driver behavior)
// would have kept {0} and over-rejected a program that leaks nothing.
fn fwd(x) {
    let r = x;
    r = 0;
    return r;
}
fn main() uses(net.send) { send("host", 80, fwd(secret_source("api_key"))); }
